llins is at 49.5 percent right now  if nobody gets above 50 they ship all  the ballots to augusta  and they look at what people's second  choice was  for senate so there is actually a  wonderfully civilized way to do it  it pushes people toward the center  instead of pushing them to the polls  it keeps an independent from being a  spoiler because they get four percent of  the vote  makes it very complicated on election  day though true it sure does and there  is an independent candidate who's  getting about 4.5 percent of the vote  she has told people  hey if i don't win put sarah gideon the  challenger is your second choice  so a lot still up in the air and then  let's take a look at the two races in  georgia  just like the presidential level we  can't make a call here yet david perdue  with a lead  over john ossoff with about 91 percent  of the vote in and then  this other georgia race is definitely  going to be going to a runoff  in january so the question now is  whether you got two races in georgia  going to a runoff  or one but either way it looks like i'm  headed to buckhead for the holidays you  have more work to do  there was a phrase that you used a  couple times there despite the polls and  i think we're going to be using that a  lot of the days  oh and i just want to point out  something to you really quickly look  over here on the democratic side of the  leisure michigan  is now a toss-up for the incumbent gary  peters if democrats can't hold on to  that seat  their path to the majority closes almost  again despite the polls we're going to  be having a bigger conversation about  that in the days ahead because this  thing is tight at the senate level and  also the presidential  level tighter than a lot of people  thought all right nancy cordes thank you  very much
 

